    "body": "The diagnostic section was hidden behind a language server check, which hides linter results.\r\n\r\nResolve #687\r\n\r\n- [x] I have read [CONTRIBUTING.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md)\r\n- [x] I have read [CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md)\r\n",
    "closed_at": "2024-04-12T08:28:30Z",
    "comment_data": [
        {
            "_links": {
                "html": {
                    "href": "https://github.com/nvim-mini/mini.nvim/pull/806#discussion_r1561975784"
                },
                "pull_request": {
                    "href": "https://api.github.com/repos/nvim-mini/mini.nvim/pulls/806"
                },
                "self": {
                    "href": "https://api.github.com/repos/nvim-mini/mini.nvim/pulls/comments/1561975784"
                }
            },
            "author_association": "NONE",
            "body": "We mentioned this section didn't feel useful in the issue. I find its nice to know if the LSP server is working and connected, but I also get this from `mini.notify`.\r\n\r\nHappy to either remove this, or keep it and write up unit tests.",
            "commit_id": "aec449daf38ed61b02f83d4b6196eb1f8b4a57c3",
            "copilot_code_review_sources": [],
            "created_at": "2024-04-12T03:39:48Z",
            "diff_hunk": "@@ -281,33 +281,46 @@ MiniStatusline.section_git = function(args)\n   return string.format('%s %s %s', icon, head, signs)\n end\n \n+--- Section for Neovim's builtin lsp\n+---\n+--- Shows nothing if there is no attached lsp\n+--- Uses LspAttach and LspDetach events to determine if an LSP is attached.\n+---\n+---@param args __statusline_args Use `args.icon` to supply your own icon.\n+---\n+---@return __statusline_section\n+MiniStatusline.section_lsp = function(args)",
